maria: For the docs page I'll include recommended debugging pattern: 1) capture req id, 2) log request/response headers, 3) attach stack + user-visible message. Example snippet for handler logs: ```go
if apiErr := errors.As(err, &APIError{}); apiErr {
  logger.WithFields(logrus.Fields{
    "req": apiErr.RequestID,
    "code": apiErr.Code,
    "status": apiErr.StatusCode,
    "raw_truncated": apiErr.RawTruncated,
  }).Error(apiErr)
}
```

aj: one more: map certain API codes to typed errors (e.g. ErrQuotaExceeded) so callers can switch on `errors.Is(err, ErrQuotaExceeded)` rather than string-match.

ken: will implement ErrQuotaExceeded as `var ErrQuotaExceeded = errors.New("quota_exceeded")` and wrap the APIError: `errors.Join(ErrQuotaExceeded, apiErr)` or provide an `As`/`Is` helper.

maria: great. i'll open PR and tag you both for review. will also add changelog and a small migration note for existing users (field rename guidance).

